aef5d17d9c90491f60ffbcaa60dd" commit_message="openresolv: upgraded package to upstream  Upgraded net-dns/openresolv to version 3.7.0 on arm  BUG=b:34770284 TEST=Compiles  Change-Id: I7c640251608fc7eec05f33656a5118caf27a8fc5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/435476 Commit-Ready: Ian Coolidge &lt;icoolidge@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Ian Coolidge &lt;icoolidge@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="5" gerrit_number="435476" owner_email="icoolidge@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/portage-stable" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/portage-stable" ref="refs/changes/76/435476/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6a1af33735c8114fd4600618f647d5adc0a89603" commit="4a8fa28a7de3216500837fb83f15f218606f36ad" commit_message="update_engine: migrate usage of deprecated base::Value methods  Methods provided by base::Value that consume or produce unmanaged raw pointers have been deprecated and will be eventually removed from libchrome. This CL migrates the usage of these deprecated methods in the update-engine code to the equivalent methods that use std::unique_ptr.  BUG=chromium:689697 TEST=Run unit tests.  Change-Id: I6a1af33735c8114fd4600618f647d5adc0a89603 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/438840 Commit-Ready: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="438840" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="aosp/platform/system/update_engine" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/update_engine" ref="refs/changes/40/438840/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib903ebb269f8dd22fa26d85acfaa87ea8b6b4be1" commit="0c16140042e68258ebf1c5e9f703202272eb0306" commit_message="frecon: Select crtc with max number of planes.  Make frecon use a similar logic to what Chrome uses to select a crtc for a connector.  In this way during the transition between the splash screen to the CrOS login page the crtc won't change and the transition will be seamless.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:62144, chrome-os-partner:59814 TEST=restarted kevin with new frecon, the transition from the splash to chrome didn't go black.  Change-Id: Ib903ebb269f8dd22fa26d85acfaa87ea8b6b4be1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/436704 Commit-Ready: Daniele Castagna &lt;dcastagna@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniele Castagna &lt;dcastagna@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniele Castagna &lt;dcastagna@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kristian H. Kristensen &lt;hoegsberg@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="436704" owner_email="dcastagna@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/frecon" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/frecon" ref="refs/changes/04/436704/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If3657091cff5727adf0dd2a15ccfa3f94095cc83" commit="7cdc1d024b1d52e7f96a2eb0f5cca9e311b4baac" commit_message="metrics: avoid overflow from bad sysfs value  A zram bug can create very large values for orig_data_size, which causes an overflow.  Rather than fixing various kernel versions, we work around the problem here.  BUG=chromium:686928 TEST=none  Change-Id: If3657091cff5727adf0dd2a15ccfa3f94095cc83 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/439005 Commit-Ready: Luigi Semenzato &lt;semenzato@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Luigi Semenzato &lt;semenzato@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="439005" owner_email="semenzato@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/05/439005/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I70e4a1e6727d2c80181dff0956f13f8cbdabd166" commit="43319d7e1c3b9b5295e31b976b9ebe595eb69062" commit_message="CHROMIUM: net: xt_qtaguid: Fix iface_create_proc_worker() races  iface_create_proc_worker() runs from a workqueue, so if an interface is brought up and then brought back down very rapidly, it could dereference a NULL new_iface-&gt;net_dev pointer and crash the kernel.  Fix this by passing a struct net in the iface_stat_work struct, instead of relying on new_iface-&gt;net_dev to be valid.  Also, the proc entries created by iface_create_proc_worker() are deleted from qtaguid_net_exit().  So iface_create_proc_worker() should hold a reference to the struct net until the entries are created, to prevent qtaguid_net_exit() from running until the worker function finishes.  The first race was seen intermittently; it involved `daisydog -c`, which runs in its own netns due to minijail, and terminates almost immediately. The worker function apparently ran after the netns was torn down.  The second race has not been seen in the wild.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:62652 TEST=manually run on kevin, check for kernel oopses  Change-Id: I70e4a1e6727d2c80181dff0956f13f8cbdabd166 Signed-off-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/437996 Tested-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit ee46482554af104a9cd77bc1816b540a57067ba4) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/439388 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="439388" owner_email="cernekee@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/88/439388/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6be2fb14676be31ae578afceda2410a4b5f6af5e" commit="25e645db0ce51c22979ad618871316d37b01f046" commit_message="Simplify capturing of base::JSONReader::Read() return value.  base::JSONReader::Read() returns a std::unique_ptr&lt;Value&gt;, which can simply be captured into a std::unique_ptr&lt;Value&gt; variable instead of calling .release() on the returned unique_ptr and constructing a unique_ptr from the released raw pointer.  BUG=None TEST=Run unit tests.  Change-Id: I6be2fb14676be31ae578afceda2410a4b5f6af5e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/438760 Commit-Ready: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="438760" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="aosp/platform/external/dbus-binding-generator" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/external/dbus-binding-generator" ref="refs/changes/60/438760/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8891d32892663e278ed976650f3fee3f06e544de" commit="9bf2d073e6548dc4bb6ddb9a30e93be1c3be90a7" commit_message="make.defualts:  ac_cv_func_{mmap_fixed_mapped,wait3_rusage}  This CL removes the following settings in profiles/targets/chromeos/make.defaults:      ac_cv_func_mmap_fixed_mapped=yes     ac_cv_func_wait3_rusage=yes  as they are already set by crossdev (since commit 1a54546d5a2e677c46825e7cc3a309d1735733b0: &quot;mmap_fixed_mapped,wait3_rusage&quot;).  BUG=None TEST=Remote trybot runs on paladin, release, and chromiumos-sdk builders.  Change-Id: I8891d32892663e278ed976650f3fee3f06e544de Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/439424 Commit-Ready: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="439424" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/24/439424/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If8fa22c5830ffbd885d66bf63e7afaf662fd1ec3" commit="f557c00a519a1f0904bb417d334a53ccfa4a7bf3" commit_message="libbrillo: migrate usage of deprecated base::Value methods  base::ListValue::DeepCopy() and base::DictionaryValue::DeepCopy() have been deprecated and will eventually be removed from libchrome. This CL migrates the usage of these deprecated methods in the libbrillo code to the equivalent base::ListValue::CreateDeepCopy() and base::DictionaryValue::CreateDeepCopy().  BUG=chromium:689697 TEST=Run unit tests.  Change-Id: If8fa22c5830ffbd885d66bf63e7afaf662fd1ec3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/438798 Commit-Ready: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="438798" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="aosp/platform/external/libbrillo" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/external/libbrillo" ref="refs/changes/98/438798/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="9263.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>